I just got Wizard mode to work on a UNIX system a few weeks ago (but
I am definitely NOT a UNIX guru).  What I think happens is when running
the game in wizard mode, the game checks your chanracter's name AND your
login id.  In the default distribution, you can't get it to work unless
your login ID happens to be izchak (or whatever the spelling is).

To fix this, edit the include/config.h file, and set the #define WIZARD
and the #define WIZARD_NAME to be your login ID.  Then recompile, and
run the game 'nethack -u your_login_id -D'  (or was it nethack -D -u
your_login_id).

My pet peave with this bit of code (src/unixmain.c) is that if it 
finds that you are not authorized to run wizard/debug mode, it drops
you into explore/discover mode without any prompting.  I think it should
tell you "Only " WIZARD "is authorized to run wizard mode -- starting in
discover mode".  Perhaps the restriction should be removed.  I don't care
if others on my system want to run the game in wizard mode.  It would be
simple to change, but I haven't bothered yet.  If anyone wants to improve
unixmain.c, please post your change.
